      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-03T17:48:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It\u0027s supposed to be used for such cases and it has both alignment and null checks\n\nBut the documentation says the exact opposite(?):\n\n\u003e Behavior is undefined if any of the following conditions are violated:\n\u003e\n\u003e - dst must be valid for writes.\n\u003e \n\u003e - dst must be properly aligned. Use write_unaligned if this is not the case.\n\u003e \n\u003e Note that even if T has size 0, the pointer must be non-null and properly aligned.\n\nand we shouldn\u0027t rely on an undocumented check in the implementation (in particular as `assert_unsafe_precondition!` can be disabled at `std`/`core` build time, IIUC).",
      "parentUuid": "69c1d1ad_3b729637",
