      "writtenOn": "2023-01-03T17:48:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s just that `from_X` methods usually return a value, not a reference, making `Payload::from_avb_ops_ptr()` unnecessarily confusing.\n\n\u003e It\u0027s also not so extendable in case we want to look at other parts of `AvbOps`.\n\nDoes the borrow checker complain if you re-use the `*AvbOps` after having created a `\u0026Payload` from it?",
